.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH localfly 1  "localfly 0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
localfly \- Your localhost, on the internet (Localfly Linux)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlocalfly\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Your localhost, on the internet (Localfly Linux)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
localfly\-add(1)
Save an app by its local port
.TP
localfly\-list(1)
List saved apps with live status dots
.TP
localfly\-rm(1)
Remove a saved app (by id prefix, name, or port)
.TP
localfly\-edit(1)
Edit a saved app
.TP
localfly\-on(1)
Expose a saved app in the daemon (follows status; Ctrl\-C detaches, tunnel keeps running)
.TP
localfly\-off(1)
Stop a saved app\*(Aqs tunnel (or \-\-all)
.TP
localfly\-expose(1)
One\-shot tunnel without saving (foreground; Ctrl\-C stops it)
.TP
localfly\-up(1)
Start every app marked start\-on\-launch in the daemon (foreground follow; SIGTERM stops all)
.TP
localfly\-status(1)
Show live tunnels and their traffic
.TP
localfly\-probe(1)
Check whether something listens on a port
.TP
localfly\-scan(1)
Scan localhost for common dev\-server ports
.TP
localfly\-relay\-status(1)
Measure relay control\-port latency
.TP
localfly\-config(1)
Persist defaults (mirrors macOS Settings: relay, auto\-reconnect, local host)
.TP
localfly\-update\-check(1)
Check GitHub releases for a newer version (read\-only, like UpdateChecker)
.TP
localfly\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.1
